CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 11 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ pack forwarded to base initializer sets the flag: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ pack forwarded to base initializer sets value: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[temp.variadic] / [class.base.init]: a constructor may forward a function
parameter pack to a base-class initializer that has a non-pack argument before
the pack expansion (`Base(tag, args...)`).  CBMC mis-classified a class with a
base and a (template) constructor as an aggregate ([dcl.init.aggr]/1 -- a class
with a user-declared constructor, including a template one, is not an
aggregate), so it aggregate-initialised the base member-wise and dropped the
pack.  This is std::optional's construction shape
(`_Optional_base(in_place, forward<Args>(args)...)`).

